1
00:00:01,133 --> 00:00:03,135
[opening theme song playing]

2
00:00:04,177 --> 00:00:07,431
BLUE BOX

3
00:01:23,673 --> 00:01:29,930
BLUE BOX

4
00:01:30,555 --> 00:01:31,473
{\an8}EPISODE 11
UNCOOL!

5
00:01:31,556 --> 00:01:34,017
{\an8}...<i>the start of summer break for many
students in our area</i>...

6
00:01:34,100 --> 00:01:34,935
{\an8}SUMMER BREAK

7
00:01:36,019 --> 00:01:36,937
Oh.

8
00:01:37,604 --> 00:01:39,064
- [muffled] Good morning.
- Morning.

9
00:01:39,689 --> 00:01:42,442
[Taiki] <i>Oh, man.
Looks like we're alone together.</i>

10
00:01:42,526 --> 00:01:44,319
<i>But it'll be weird if I just leave.</i>

11
00:01:45,070 --> 00:01:46,571
Do you have practice today?

12
00:01:46,655 --> 00:01:48,406
Um, what was that?

13
00:01:48,490 --> 00:01:49,491
Practice.

14
00:01:49,574 --> 00:01:50,826
Uh...

15
00:01:52,119 --> 00:01:54,371
[gargles, spits]

16
00:01:55,330 --> 00:01:58,291
Badminton practice?
You're not wearing your sports gear.

17
00:01:58,375 --> 00:01:59,584
Oh. Uh. Yeah.

18
00:02:00,544 --> 00:02:02,796
But I'm meeting friends
at the library later,

19
00:02:02,879 --> 00:02:04,756
so we can do summer-break homework.

20
00:02:05,298 --> 00:02:06,800
That's why I'm wearing this.

21
00:02:06,883 --> 00:02:09,094
[Chinatsu] Oh. Sounds like a good time.

22
00:02:09,177 --> 00:02:11,638
[chuckles] I might
have to steal your idea.

23
00:02:13,473 --> 00:02:14,891
Well, good luck, then.

24
00:02:15,934 --> 00:02:17,102
Yeah thanks.

25
00:02:19,729 --> 00:02:21,648
[Taiki] <i>She's acting super normal.</i>

26
00:02:23,692 --> 00:02:25,610
{\an8}EIMEI PRIVATE HIGH SCHOOL

27
00:02:25,694 --> 00:02:27,237
<i>- I guess that's that.</i>
- [Haryu] Yo.

28
00:02:27,320 --> 00:02:28,155
Hey!

29
00:02:28,238 --> 00:02:30,615
<i>I should just forget about it and move on.</i>

30
00:02:30,699 --> 00:02:33,994
So, I won't do anything like that again,

31
00:02:34,077 --> 00:02:35,120
going forward.

32
00:02:35,704 --> 00:02:38,123
[Taiki] <i>I'm right back to where I started.</i>

33
00:02:45,213 --> 00:02:47,340
[snoring]

34
00:02:47,424 --> 00:02:50,302
- [Taiki] No sleeping, Hina!
- I wasn't asleep!

35
00:02:50,385 --> 00:02:54,097
We all made the time to get together,
so let's focus up and work.

36
00:02:54,180 --> 00:02:58,351
Yeah, but I heard that sleep is when
your brain makes all your memories stick.

37
00:02:58,435 --> 00:02:59,394
So you were sleeping.

38
00:03:00,020 --> 00:03:02,981
I'm looking at all these numbers,
but I don't get any of it.

39
00:03:03,064 --> 00:03:04,524
No one taught me this stuff.

40
00:03:04,608 --> 00:03:05,901
Well, actually, they did.

41
00:03:05,984 --> 00:03:08,486
Well, if you just substitute that for x...

42
00:03:08,570 --> 00:03:10,155
- [boy] Yo dude.
- What?

43
00:03:10,238 --> 00:03:13,450
- So...
- Look at Ito, he's making a move.

44
00:03:13,533 --> 00:03:16,661
It's about time.
He's been crushing on her forever.

45
00:03:16,745 --> 00:03:20,206
They won't run into each other
anymore because of summer break,

46
00:03:20,290 --> 00:03:22,876
so today's the day.
At least get her number, dude.

47
00:03:22,959 --> 00:03:25,921
- [Taiki exclaiming]
- [Kyo] Just do your homework.

48
00:03:27,255 --> 00:03:29,424
[Taiki] <i>I guess I haven't thought
about it before but...</i>

49
00:03:30,091 --> 00:03:32,594
<i>everyone's got a crush on someone.</i>

50
00:03:41,561 --> 00:03:43,188
[Taiki] What's up, slacker.

51
00:03:43,271 --> 00:03:46,441
I'm not a slacker, I'm here
'cause I'm fresh out of energy.

52
00:03:47,317 --> 00:03:49,444
[Taiki] Doesn't mean
you should sleep here.

53
00:03:49,527 --> 00:03:51,696
Oh, look who just sat down.

54
00:03:51,780 --> 00:03:54,449
Uh-huh, 'cause we can't have
drinks in the library.

55
00:03:54,532 --> 00:03:56,910
[gulps] Ah, that hits the spot.

56
00:03:57,494 --> 00:04:01,206
[girl 1 squeals] I can't believe
the fireworks festival is next week!

57
00:04:01,289 --> 00:04:03,708
[girl 2] Yeah! We're all
still going together right?

58
00:04:03,792 --> 00:04:05,835
Of course! And let's invite Sasaki.

59
00:04:05,919 --> 00:04:06,962
[chuckles] For sure!

60
00:04:07,545 --> 00:04:08,964
In junior high,

61
00:04:09,047 --> 00:04:10,924
we went to the festival together.

62
00:04:11,591 --> 00:04:13,510
Yeah, that was all Saijo's idea.

63
00:04:14,052 --> 00:04:15,845
I wonder how that kid's doing.

64
00:04:16,721 --> 00:04:18,473
[Taiki] He's at San High,
and joined a band.

65
00:04:18,556 --> 00:04:20,350
I can totally see that.

66
00:04:20,433 --> 00:04:23,353
That's also about the time
when you and I started talking.

67
00:04:24,646 --> 00:04:25,689
Was it?

68
00:04:27,941 --> 00:04:30,360
[Saijo] There's a fireworks festival
next week!

69
00:04:31,152 --> 00:04:33,280
We'll be classmates
for all of junior high,

70
00:04:33,363 --> 00:04:35,365
so let's commemorate it and go together!

71
00:04:35,448 --> 00:04:37,367
- [boy] Sounds good to me!
- You gonna go Hina?

72
00:04:37,993 --> 00:04:40,245
[Hina] <i>I want a candy apple.</i>

73
00:04:40,328 --> 00:04:41,997
I guess you're going.

74
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:44,082
But don't we have practice that day?

75
00:04:45,875 --> 00:04:48,586
It'll be fine. Practice ends at 6:00.

76
00:04:48,670 --> 00:04:51,172
You can only get candy apples
at festivals like this!

77
00:04:51,256 --> 00:04:53,383
Okay. Raise your hand if you're going!

78
00:04:53,466 --> 00:04:56,219
- Me!
- Oh! [groans]

79
00:04:56,303 --> 00:04:59,639
- All right then...
- Oops. Sorry about that, Taiki.

80
00:04:59,723 --> 00:05:01,433
Oh, it's all right.

81
00:05:01,516 --> 00:05:02,934
Ah, but...

82
00:05:03,018 --> 00:05:05,395
- It's all good, Hina, really.
- [Hina] Hm.

83
00:05:05,478 --> 00:05:07,897
Geez, Hina. What was that all about?

84
00:05:07,981 --> 00:05:09,149
Nothing.

85
00:05:09,232 --> 00:05:11,735
I'm just too excited. That's all.

86
00:05:13,236 --> 00:05:14,654
GYMNASTICS CLUB

87
00:05:14,738 --> 00:05:16,156
JULY

88
00:05:16,239 --> 00:05:17,657
{\an8}WINNER

89
00:05:23,747 --> 00:05:25,040
[panting]

90
00:05:26,249 --> 00:05:29,169
<i>I'm running so late.
Why'd it have to be today?</i>

91
00:05:29,753 --> 00:05:31,588
<i>I don't wanna miss a single second!</i>

92
00:05:37,761 --> 00:05:40,138
[sighs] <i>It started already.</i>

93
00:05:43,767 --> 00:05:45,935
I guess I'll try to find the others.

94
00:05:46,019 --> 00:05:47,437
CANDY APPLES

95
00:05:47,520 --> 00:05:48,688
SOLD OUT

96
00:05:49,481 --> 00:05:52,025
<i>No way! That was all I cared about!</i>

97
00:05:57,781 --> 00:05:58,740
<i>Oh, well.</i>

98
00:05:59,365 --> 00:06:03,203
<i>I need to make sacrifices
so I can do my best in gymnastics.</i>

99
00:06:04,079 --> 00:06:07,874
<i>I should give up going out with friends
and trying the food stands,</i>

100
00:06:07,957 --> 00:06:09,375
<i>eating candy apples...</i>

101
00:06:10,585 --> 00:06:11,669
<i>Give up...</i>

102
00:06:15,465 --> 00:06:16,591
Here you go.

103
00:06:17,175 --> 00:06:18,093
[gasps]

104
00:06:20,386 --> 00:06:22,514
They sent me to buy stuff for everybody.

105
00:06:22,597 --> 00:06:24,891
And this was the last one. Here.

106
00:06:24,974 --> 00:06:26,351
Well, thank you.

107
00:06:27,143 --> 00:06:29,729
But how did you even know
that I wanted one?

108
00:06:29,813 --> 00:06:31,815
I happened to notice
you were drooling before.

109
00:06:31,898 --> 00:06:34,234
Wait! You saw that?

110
00:06:34,317 --> 00:06:36,778
I sure did. You made such a weird face.

111
00:06:36,861 --> 00:06:39,364
Hey! Leave me alone!

112
00:06:39,948 --> 00:06:41,157
Look at us now.

113
00:06:41,241 --> 00:06:44,160
And you're still committing
acts of violence against me.

114
00:06:44,244 --> 00:06:45,370
What?

115
00:06:46,162 --> 00:06:47,497
We've been so busy

116
00:06:47,580 --> 00:06:50,083
that we haven't gone
to the festival since.

117
00:06:50,166 --> 00:06:51,918
I forgot how much fun we had.

118
00:06:52,460 --> 00:06:54,129
[slow music playing]

119
00:06:56,548 --> 00:06:57,757
I should get back.

120
00:06:59,759 --> 00:07:01,386
So let's go again.

121
00:07:02,053 --> 00:07:02,971
[Taiki] Hm?

122
00:07:05,974 --> 00:07:07,851
This year, you and me.

123
00:07:10,353 --> 00:07:11,896
We should go together.

124
00:07:13,064 --> 00:07:14,899
[slow music ends]

125
00:07:15,900 --> 00:07:17,902
Let's go to the fireworks festival.

126
00:07:18,695 --> 00:07:19,654
[exclaims softly]

127
00:07:24,075 --> 00:07:25,034
Sure.

128
00:07:25,869 --> 00:07:26,828
For real?

129
00:07:27,454 --> 00:07:30,623
Inomata! I think
you just missed a phone call.

130
00:07:30,707 --> 00:07:32,417
The buzzing was getting annoying.

131
00:07:32,500 --> 00:07:34,669
[Taiki] Oh, thanks. Sorry about that.

132
00:07:36,629 --> 00:07:38,047
We'll talk details later.

133
00:07:38,882 --> 00:07:40,049
Yeah, sounds good.

134
00:07:40,967 --> 00:07:43,052
- Why don't we head back?
- Yeah.

135
00:07:43,595 --> 00:07:45,054
FIREWORKS FESTIVAL

136
00:07:46,055 --> 00:07:48,558
[Niina] Oh, look, the fireworks festival
is coming up.

137
00:07:48,641 --> 00:07:51,060
- What are you doing? Wanna go together?
- [Hina] Ah...

138
00:07:51,811 --> 00:07:55,356
I'm sorry, Niina, I went and made plans
with someone else already.

139
00:07:56,524 --> 00:07:58,067
With who?

140
00:07:58,776 --> 00:08:00,195
So is it a date or...

141
00:08:00,278 --> 00:08:01,613
[Hina] No!

142
00:08:01,696 --> 00:08:05,074
[Niina] Guy plus girl plus fireworks...
Definitely a date.

143
00:08:05,158 --> 00:08:07,076
It isn't like that. Really.

144
00:08:07,160 --> 00:08:09,579
He's only ever thought of me
as his friend.

145
00:08:09,662 --> 00:08:10,872
[Niina chuckles]

146
00:08:11,623 --> 00:08:13,082
Well, I hope you have fun.

147
00:08:13,666 --> 00:08:14,792
[exclaims softly]

148
00:08:18,838 --> 00:08:22,175
- [Niina] Sorry that I interrupted earlier.
- There's nothing going on with Taiki!

149
00:08:22,258 --> 00:08:23,593
[Niina] Yeah, okay.

150
00:08:23,676 --> 00:08:25,595
[insects trilling]

151
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:31,100
[Yukiko] Three weeks until
Chinatsu goes to nationals, huh?

152
00:08:32,268 --> 00:08:35,104
- So, are you feeling ready?
- As I'll ever be.

153
00:08:35,813 --> 00:08:37,941
Do let me know if you need anything, okay?

154
00:08:38,566 --> 00:08:40,401
You'll be there a few nights, right?

155
00:08:40,485 --> 00:08:42,487
I can buy what you need
if you make me a list.

156
00:08:43,071 --> 00:08:44,489
I really appreciate it.

157
00:08:46,074 --> 00:08:49,285
Oh. The fireworks festival
is next weekend.

158
00:08:49,911 --> 00:08:51,287
Do you think you'll go?

159
00:08:51,371 --> 00:08:53,039
I might stop by for a bit.

160
00:08:53,122 --> 00:08:54,958
{\an8}I have a <i>yukata</i> for you.

161
00:08:56,209 --> 00:09:00,505
[Taiki] <i>I am trying to keep my distance
over here and focus on my homework!</i>

162
00:09:00,588 --> 00:09:03,466
<i>How could you bring up such a distraction?</i>

163
00:09:03,550 --> 00:09:05,802
[Yukiko] <i>It's a bit old,
but really pretty.</i>

164
00:09:05,885 --> 00:09:07,637
[Chinatsu] <i>Oh, no. I'm okay.</i>

165
00:09:07,720 --> 00:09:08,930
[grunts]

166
00:09:10,223 --> 00:09:12,433
- [Yukiko] What about you, Taiki?
- Mm?

167
00:09:12,517 --> 00:09:14,394
Are you going to go to the festival?

168
00:09:15,186 --> 00:09:16,813
Yeah, with some friends.

169
00:09:16,896 --> 00:09:18,940
Don't do anything wild, okay?

170
00:09:19,482 --> 00:09:21,943
[Taiki] <i>Actually, who else is even coming?</i>

171
00:09:22,735 --> 00:09:25,154
<i>I should probably see if Kyo can come.</i>

172
00:09:25,822 --> 00:09:28,658
<i>Hina is not really the organizing type.</i>

173
00:09:28,741 --> 00:09:31,452
All right, then the rest of us
will go over to Yokoi's,

174
00:09:31,536 --> 00:09:33,162
and watch the fireworks from there.

175
00:09:33,246 --> 00:09:35,081
But that's the ultimate viewing spot mom!

176
00:09:35,164 --> 00:09:36,874
I'll have to bring some booze!

177
00:09:36,958 --> 00:09:38,167
Don't rub it in my face!

178
00:09:38,251 --> 00:09:41,170
- [Yukiko] We are adults after all.
- Well, we're gonna have soft drinks!

179
00:09:41,254 --> 00:09:43,172
[shuttlecock thudding]

180
00:09:55,226 --> 00:09:56,185
[pants]

181
00:09:56,769 --> 00:09:59,689
That was a productive practice.
Thanks, Taiki.

182
00:10:00,273 --> 00:10:03,192
[Taiki] <i>Somehow
Haryu's gotten even better lately.</i>

183
00:10:03,276 --> 00:10:04,110
[Haryu sighs]

184
00:10:04,193 --> 00:10:07,822
[Taiki] <i>The way things are going,
I'll never catch up to him.</i>

185
00:10:07,905 --> 00:10:09,949
- By the way...
- What do you want now?

186
00:10:10,033 --> 00:10:12,118
You already beat me, don't make it worse.

187
00:10:12,201 --> 00:10:14,120
You don't have to be so hostile, bro.

188
00:10:14,203 --> 00:10:15,204
I'm not hostile!

189
00:10:16,164 --> 00:10:17,749
So on the 31st,

190
00:10:17,832 --> 00:10:20,209
I'll be meeting up
with a friend of mine at his practice.

191
00:10:20,293 --> 00:10:23,212
He's on the university team. Wanna come?

192
00:10:23,296 --> 00:10:25,214
University team?

193
00:10:25,298 --> 00:10:28,468
Yeah they're ranked pretty high up,
so it's gonna be intense.

194
00:10:28,551 --> 00:10:29,886
I'll be there!

195
00:10:30,553 --> 00:10:31,971
[water running]

196
00:10:39,604 --> 00:10:41,064
- [turns off tap]
- [chuckles softly]

197
00:10:42,940 --> 00:10:43,941
[yelps]

198
00:10:44,025 --> 00:10:45,735
Why are you grinning at yourself?

199
00:10:45,818 --> 00:10:48,946
Hina! Do you always
need to sneak up on me?

200
00:10:49,030 --> 00:10:51,741
You were smiling in the mirror,
and I couldn't help myself.

201
00:10:51,824 --> 00:10:54,702
You spend a lot of your time
goofy-grinning, you know.

202
00:10:54,786 --> 00:10:56,996
- You're such a daydreamer.
- Nuh-uh!

203
00:10:57,622 --> 00:11:00,792
I was invited
to practice with a university team.

204
00:11:00,875 --> 00:11:02,585
So I'm just feeling excited.

205
00:11:04,504 --> 00:11:07,131
I have to make the most
of this opportunity

206
00:11:07,215 --> 00:11:09,258
with everyone about to go to nationals.

207
00:11:10,009 --> 00:11:12,303
It's the same day
as the fireworks festival,

208
00:11:12,387 --> 00:11:14,347
but I'll be there in time, okay?

209
00:11:14,430 --> 00:11:15,556
[Hina] Okay.

210
00:11:15,640 --> 00:11:17,433
I have practice, too, anyway.

211
00:11:18,935 --> 00:11:20,269
[Taiki] I can't wait.

212
00:11:21,187 --> 00:11:23,856
These festivals have the best <i>yakisoba.</i>

213
00:11:23,940 --> 00:11:25,483
Must be the grills they use.

214
00:11:25,566 --> 00:11:27,652
So carbs before beauty, right?

215
00:11:27,735 --> 00:11:28,778
By the way,

216
00:11:28,861 --> 00:11:30,780
who else is gonna be in our group?

217
00:11:30,863 --> 00:11:31,781
Huh?

218
00:11:32,407 --> 00:11:33,324
[grunts]

219
00:11:33,866 --> 00:11:36,160
Uh... uh...

220
00:11:36,869 --> 00:11:39,705
I forgot to invite other people. Whoopsie!

221
00:11:39,789 --> 00:11:40,748
For real?

222
00:11:40,832 --> 00:11:43,459
Taiki, why don't you go ahead
and invite Kyo for me?

223
00:11:43,543 --> 00:11:45,837
And I'll reach out to my friends
and see who can make it.

224
00:11:45,920 --> 00:11:47,130
Thanks for your help.

225
00:11:49,048 --> 00:11:51,300
[Taiki] <i>She paused. What was that?</i>

226
00:11:57,890 --> 00:12:00,309
[whimpers]

227
00:12:03,396 --> 00:12:05,731
Can't believe I messed up asking him out.

228
00:12:07,108 --> 00:12:10,027
The fireworks festival?
Sure, I'm down to join you.

229
00:12:10,570 --> 00:12:11,946
It's gonna be great.

230
00:12:12,029 --> 00:12:13,406
Let's meet at 6:00.

231
00:12:13,489 --> 00:12:16,826
Wait, I thought you were going
to the university practice

232
00:12:16,909 --> 00:12:17,994
with Haryu that day.

233
00:12:18,077 --> 00:12:20,329
It's okay, I can make it to both of them.

234
00:12:20,955 --> 00:12:25,710
[Kyo] Aren't you a busy man,
squeezing two big events into one day.

235
00:12:25,793 --> 00:12:28,588
[Taiki] It's just one day.
And I wanna go to both.

236
00:12:29,630 --> 00:12:32,133
So who else is coming
with us to the festival?

237
00:12:32,216 --> 00:12:33,342
[Taiki] Hina, for one.

238
00:12:34,552 --> 00:12:36,345
It was her idea, actually.

239
00:12:36,429 --> 00:12:39,515
Although, it sounds like
she forgot to invite other people,

240
00:12:39,599 --> 00:12:41,851
so she told me to invite you.

241
00:12:41,934 --> 00:12:45,354
[Kyo] <i>That's probably because
she wanted to go with you, alone!</i>

242
00:12:46,063 --> 00:12:48,191
All right! Let's get going.

243
00:12:48,274 --> 00:12:50,401
[Kyo] <i>I mean, good for her
for mustering up</i>

244
00:12:50,485 --> 00:12:52,195
<i>the courage to ask him out at all.</i>

245
00:12:53,362 --> 00:12:57,033
<i>But getting psyched up to go for it
is useless if she's not clear!</i>

246
00:12:57,116 --> 00:12:58,701
<i>She's made a mess of this.</i>

247
00:12:59,327 --> 00:13:01,746
What? What do you mean
you already made plans

248
00:13:01,829 --> 00:13:04,248
to go to the fireworks festival
with your hometown friends?

249
00:13:04,832 --> 00:13:07,460
Well, yeah, you said
you'd found someone to go with.

250
00:13:07,543 --> 00:13:09,587
True, but you could've spent
a little more time

251
00:13:09,670 --> 00:13:12,298
feeling bad about the fact
that you couldn't go with me!

252
00:13:12,381 --> 00:13:13,508
Okay, rude.

253
00:13:14,509 --> 00:13:16,886
Did something happen
with the guy you asked out?

254
00:13:16,969 --> 00:13:18,513
Don't tell me he said no.

255
00:13:19,096 --> 00:13:20,515
We are going together.

256
00:13:21,224 --> 00:13:23,893
But he, apparently,
thinks we're going as a group.

257
00:13:24,477 --> 00:13:25,978
Go clarify with him.

258
00:13:26,062 --> 00:13:27,522
Say you just meant you two.

259
00:13:28,314 --> 00:13:29,524
No way.

260
00:13:30,149 --> 00:13:34,278
Just asking him if we could go together
used up all the courage I have, Niina.

261
00:13:34,362 --> 00:13:36,030
And if he turns me down,

262
00:13:36,113 --> 00:13:38,324
that could potentially
affect our friendship.

263
00:13:39,784 --> 00:13:41,035
[sighs]

264
00:13:41,869 --> 00:13:44,121
It's your fault for still playing
the best friend role.

265
00:13:44,205 --> 00:13:45,206
Wait, my fault?

266
00:13:45,289 --> 00:13:48,793
Hang on, you said "best friend."
Who do you think we're talking about!

267
00:13:48,876 --> 00:13:51,379
[Niina] <i>Is she actually trying
to keep it a secret?</i>

268
00:13:53,464 --> 00:13:55,007
So about the festival.

269
00:13:55,633 --> 00:13:56,592
[Chinatsu] Yeah.

270
00:13:56,676 --> 00:14:00,471
[Nagisa] As of right now, Mariko, Sana,
and Akari are planning on coming.

271
00:14:00,555 --> 00:14:01,764
[Chinatsu] Awesome!

272
00:14:02,640 --> 00:14:05,142
So should we... invite guys?

273
00:14:06,060 --> 00:14:09,981
You never know, maybe a couple of us
will hit it off in the romance department.

274
00:14:10,690 --> 00:14:13,025
And they can be shields
so we don't get hit on.

275
00:14:13,109 --> 00:14:14,151
[Chinatsu] Mm.

276
00:14:14,819 --> 00:14:16,529
Just girls is fine with me.

277
00:14:17,780 --> 00:14:21,075
I think it'll be harder
to get a good spot in a big group.

278
00:14:21,158 --> 00:14:23,828
Yeah you're right.
Okay, we'll make it just us girls then.

279
00:14:23,911 --> 00:14:27,915
[Chinatsu] <i>Besides, that isn't really
something I need right now.</i>

280
00:14:33,796 --> 00:14:34,714
[Hina] Taiki!

281
00:14:34,797 --> 00:14:35,756
Hm?

282
00:14:37,341 --> 00:14:38,718
Getting more birdies?

283
00:14:39,260 --> 00:14:40,970
We burn through 'em pretty quick.

284
00:14:41,053 --> 00:14:44,098
Summer practices are pretty long
for both of us, aren't they?

285
00:14:44,932 --> 00:14:46,392
With nationals coming up,

286
00:14:47,143 --> 00:14:48,853
be careful not to get injured.

287
00:14:48,936 --> 00:14:49,979
Mm-hm.

288
00:14:50,813 --> 00:14:54,358
Plus, there's the fireworks festival
to look forward to.

289
00:14:55,151 --> 00:14:57,111
Oh, yeah, Kyo can come with us.

290
00:14:57,194 --> 00:14:58,029
Great!

291
00:14:58,112 --> 00:14:59,155
That's just great.

292
00:14:59,238 --> 00:15:00,573
What about you?

293
00:15:00,656 --> 00:15:01,908
Did you invite anyone?

294
00:15:02,575 --> 00:15:04,869
It sounds like everyone I know
has a lot of friends.

295
00:15:04,952 --> 00:15:06,579
{\an8}[chuckles]

296
00:15:06,662 --> 00:15:08,372
{\an8}So the same group as always, then.

297
00:15:11,751 --> 00:15:13,669
Taiki, be honest with me.

298
00:15:14,462 --> 00:15:16,631
Did you actually want to go with Chinatsu?

299
00:15:20,217 --> 00:15:21,886
It wouldn't have worked.

300
00:15:21,969 --> 00:15:25,514
{\an8}We could never go to a place
as crowded as a festival,

301
00:15:25,598 --> 00:15:27,391
{\an8}because someone could spot us together.

302
00:15:28,017 --> 00:15:29,560
{\an8}And even if I asked her out,

303
00:15:29,644 --> 00:15:31,646
{\an8}I'm certain that
she would've turned me down.

304
00:15:31,729 --> 00:15:35,232
{\an8}Because she told you that the two of you
should keep your distance?

305
00:15:35,983 --> 00:15:38,569
{\an8}No need to revisit that unpleasant moment.

306
00:15:39,904 --> 00:15:44,200
I thought that she and I had gotten close
over the past few months.

307
00:15:44,283 --> 00:15:46,661
I just wanted to get even closer to her.

308
00:15:47,954 --> 00:15:50,915
But it was only me
who was feeling that way.

309
00:15:52,249 --> 00:15:55,920
I don't really understand where
the boundaries are so I don't overstep.

310
00:15:56,504 --> 00:16:00,675
I'm scared that one wrong move
is going to make her not like me.

311
00:16:00,758 --> 00:16:02,259
Or that I'll come face-to-face again

312
00:16:02,343 --> 00:16:05,429
with the fact that
I'm the only one with feelings.

313
00:16:08,307 --> 00:16:09,433
<i>And what's worse...</i>

314
00:16:09,517 --> 00:16:13,521
<i>is that the closer I get to her,
the bigger that fear gets.</i>

315
00:16:15,272 --> 00:16:16,482
Huh?

316
00:16:16,565 --> 00:16:18,943
- Let's go the other way.
- What?

317
00:16:19,527 --> 00:16:21,654
Uh... [sighs]

318
00:16:26,283 --> 00:16:27,201
[groans]

319
00:16:28,327 --> 00:16:30,287
Hey, that was really violent,
even for you--

320
00:16:30,371 --> 00:16:31,706
- This isn't like you!
- Huh?

321
00:16:32,498 --> 00:16:34,959
I get you not wanting
to bother the girl you like,

322
00:16:35,584 --> 00:16:38,337
and not wanting
to ruin your friendship with her.

323
00:16:38,421 --> 00:16:41,799
I get how those thoughts are making you
afraid to move forward...

324
00:16:42,800 --> 00:16:43,884
But Taiki...

325
00:16:44,635 --> 00:16:47,555
you looking out for others' feelings
as well as your own...

326
00:16:48,264 --> 00:16:49,724
and always staying positive...

327
00:16:50,516 --> 00:16:51,559
that's what...

328
00:16:53,227 --> 00:16:54,478
[stammers]

329
00:16:55,730 --> 00:16:57,732
that's what makes you great.

330
00:16:59,984 --> 00:17:02,611
But you're a loser
for sneaking around and avoiding her!

331
00:17:02,695 --> 00:17:03,863
Uncool!

332
00:17:03,946 --> 00:17:04,864
See you later.

333
00:17:08,868 --> 00:17:10,494
<i>Geez, what's up with her?</i>

334
00:17:11,203 --> 00:17:13,497
<i>I've never seen her like that before.</i>

335
00:17:18,210 --> 00:17:19,587
[Haryu] Taiki. Over here!

336
00:17:24,216 --> 00:17:25,551
Hi, everyone.

337
00:17:25,634 --> 00:17:26,761
[Taiki gasps]

338
00:17:28,637 --> 00:17:30,264
Hyodo?

339
00:17:31,015 --> 00:17:32,224
Why's he here?

340
00:17:32,933 --> 00:17:34,769
He's gonna be a student here next year,

341
00:17:34,852 --> 00:17:37,813
so he's coming in to practice
with them from time to time.

342
00:17:38,481 --> 00:17:40,232
[inaudible]

343
00:17:40,316 --> 00:17:42,109
[inspirational music playing]

344
00:17:45,946 --> 00:17:46,906
[grunts]

345
00:17:49,283 --> 00:17:50,451
[pants]

346
00:17:50,534 --> 00:17:51,869
This is intense.

347
00:17:51,952 --> 00:17:53,621
Way beyond our normal practice.

348
00:17:54,705 --> 00:17:57,500
Even Haryu looks like he's exhausted.

349
00:17:59,835 --> 00:18:00,753
Want some?

350
00:18:00,836 --> 00:18:02,379
Because you're staring.

351
00:18:02,463 --> 00:18:03,631
It does have my germs.

352
00:18:03,714 --> 00:18:05,257
Oh, no! I'm fine, thank you!

353
00:18:05,341 --> 00:18:06,425
Cool. Nevermind.

354
00:18:06,509 --> 00:18:08,219
[Taiki] <i>He seems pretty friendly.</i>

355
00:18:08,302 --> 00:18:11,722
You know, you tend to get tense
whenever you're under pressure.

356
00:18:11,806 --> 00:18:12,640
Huh?

357
00:18:13,224 --> 00:18:16,435
You were pulling back your right elbow
right before you'd strike.

358
00:18:17,103 --> 00:18:19,939
Stay relaxed till the shuttle
actually hits your strings.

359
00:18:20,022 --> 00:18:20,856
[Taiki] Like this?

360
00:18:20,940 --> 00:18:21,982
Yeah, that's it.

361
00:18:22,066 --> 00:18:25,653
Loosen your wrist, and focus on the angle
instead of on power.

362
00:18:26,695 --> 00:18:28,155
Hey, can you feed him one?

363
00:18:29,031 --> 00:18:30,157
You got it.

364
00:18:32,493 --> 00:18:33,661
[grunts]

365
00:18:35,788 --> 00:18:37,498
[Taiki] <i>That felt great!</i>

366
00:18:37,581 --> 00:18:38,916
Nice shot, dude.

367
00:18:38,999 --> 00:18:40,209
[Taiki exclaims softly]

368
00:18:40,292 --> 00:18:43,921
If you'd swung like that before,
you could've scored more points on Yusa.

369
00:18:47,007 --> 00:18:50,928
In your doubles matches, I thought
you got in some pretty good shots.

370
00:18:51,554 --> 00:18:54,306
But in singles,
you were stiff and always on defense.

371
00:18:54,390 --> 00:18:57,518
The way you were constantly moving around
was a total waste.

372
00:18:58,269 --> 00:19:00,437
There are two slots
for nationals next year.

373
00:19:00,521 --> 00:19:02,106
If you stay where you're at...

374
00:19:03,065 --> 00:19:05,943
my money's on Haryu and Yusa to go.
What do you think?

375
00:19:07,194 --> 00:19:09,280
[Taiki] <i>Why is he asking me about this?</i>

376
00:19:11,574 --> 00:19:12,825
I guess I agree.

377
00:19:13,784 --> 00:19:15,828
And that makes my own goals clearer.

378
00:19:17,037 --> 00:19:21,584
Haryu is my practice partner.
He represents what I want to become.

379
00:19:22,543 --> 00:19:24,587
<i>And after losing the other day,</i>

380
00:19:24,670 --> 00:19:27,464
<i>Yusa is the one
I want to beat in a rematch.</i>

381
00:19:28,424 --> 00:19:32,094
Knowing what I need to focus on...
It's good to have that clarity.

382
00:19:33,053 --> 00:19:35,472
I'm no match for either of them
at this point.

383
00:19:35,556 --> 00:19:36,473
[grunts]

384
00:19:37,349 --> 00:19:39,852
But I'm better
when I have a goal to chase down.

385
00:19:41,061 --> 00:19:42,104
[gasps softly]

386
00:19:43,564 --> 00:19:46,025
How 'bout you warn me next time? Yeah?

387
00:19:46,108 --> 00:19:48,485
[Taiki] I'm sorry! I can feed next.

388
00:19:49,111 --> 00:19:52,531
[Hyodo] <i>He makes some good points,
but he's barely got a fighting chance.</i>

389
00:19:52,615 --> 00:19:55,159
<i>The ones other players
strive to be are on top</i>

390
00:19:55,242 --> 00:19:57,453
<i>'cause they know how to deliver.</i>

391
00:19:57,536 --> 00:19:58,495
<i>But...</i>

392
00:19:59,955 --> 00:20:03,292
<i>everybody loves to root
for the underdog, don't they?</i>

393
00:20:03,375 --> 00:20:04,501
[inspirational music ends]

394
00:20:06,629 --> 00:20:08,631
[trembling]

395
00:20:11,217 --> 00:20:12,343
Nice effort today.

396
00:20:13,010 --> 00:20:14,178
Come by any time.

397
00:20:15,221 --> 00:20:16,555
Did Hyodo leave?

398
00:20:16,639 --> 00:20:17,765
[boy] Yeah, he went home.

399
00:20:19,350 --> 00:20:21,727
[Haryu] <i>The next time I see him
will be at nationals.</i>

400
00:20:23,395 --> 00:20:25,689
Taiki, got any plans?

401
00:20:25,773 --> 00:20:28,275
I'm supposed to meet Kyo and Hina at 6:00.

402
00:20:29,109 --> 00:20:31,278
KYO
SORRY, GOT A FEVER. CAN'T GO TODAY

403
00:20:31,362 --> 00:20:32,529
A fever?

404
00:20:32,613 --> 00:20:33,572
Hey, bro!

405
00:20:33,656 --> 00:20:35,032
Are you feeling okay?

406
00:20:35,115 --> 00:20:36,659
YOU OKAY?

407
00:20:36,742 --> 00:20:38,160
KYO
YOU PASSED IT ON TO ME

408
00:20:38,244 --> 00:20:39,119
WHEN?

409
00:20:39,203 --> 00:20:40,287
KYO
YOU TWO HAVE FUN

410
00:20:40,371 --> 00:20:41,288
[gasps]

411
00:20:41,914 --> 00:20:43,582
[inaudible]

412
00:20:43,666 --> 00:20:45,793
[slow music playing]

413
00:20:46,377 --> 00:20:48,003
Okay, calm down. Calm down.

414
00:20:48,087 --> 00:20:50,923
The two of us have been
hanging out alone for years now!

415
00:20:51,882 --> 00:20:53,801
HINA
I'M STILL IN

416
00:20:58,138 --> 00:21:00,057
[Taiki] <i>This place is a zoo.</i>

417
00:21:01,141 --> 00:21:03,185
<i>I wonder if I'm even gonna find her.</i>

418
00:21:06,897 --> 00:21:08,148
HINA
SORRY, RUNNING LATE!

419
00:21:08,232 --> 00:21:09,900
<i>It's one thing after another.</i>

420
00:21:09,984 --> 00:21:12,319
<i>Well, she did say
she had practice today, too.</i>

421
00:21:14,697 --> 00:21:15,823
[gasps]

422
00:21:18,325 --> 00:21:19,785
<i>My heart almost stopped.</i>

423
00:21:21,245 --> 00:21:22,121
[sighs]

424
00:21:23,205 --> 00:21:24,581
<i>That really freaked me out.</i>

425
00:21:24,665 --> 00:21:27,584
<i>I've got goals
in the romance department, too.</i>

426
00:21:27,668 --> 00:21:28,919
<i>But it's harder than badminton,</i>

427
00:21:29,003 --> 00:21:30,838
<i>'cause the other person
has to feel the same.</i>

428
00:21:30,921 --> 00:21:32,423
{\an8}CANDY APPLES
300 YEN

429
00:21:32,506 --> 00:21:34,883
{\an8}<i>If memory serves, Hina likes those.</i>

430
00:21:37,177 --> 00:21:38,345
<i>Why don't I get her one!</i>

431
00:21:38,971 --> 00:21:41,223
[woman] Here you are. Thank you very much.

432
00:21:41,890 --> 00:21:43,851
[Hina] Is that... for me?

433
00:21:44,518 --> 00:21:47,354
You better believe
you're gonna pay me back, tho-- [gasps]

434
00:21:47,438 --> 00:21:50,441
[slow music climaxes]

435
00:21:53,569 --> 00:21:54,403
What is it?

436
00:21:55,904 --> 00:21:56,739
Uh...

437
00:21:57,906 --> 00:21:58,866
It... was...

438
00:22:00,242 --> 00:22:01,785
You owe me 300 yen.

439
00:22:02,745 --> 00:22:03,579
[Hina] Okay.

440
00:22:05,456 --> 00:22:07,458
[closing theme song playing]
